# Private working directory — canonical per-publication local-only
# tree. Holds the publication's resume document
# (private/RESUME_PROMPT.md, instantiated from
# general-repo/templates/RESUME_PROMPT_TEMPLATE.md), the launch pack
# (private/launch_pack/), the dissemination workbench
# (private/dissemination/), and any feedback / session notes / audit
# outputs. See methodology/public_private_boundary_protocol.md
# ("Private working directory pattern"). Seeded projects inherit this
# line via scripts/seed_project.py copying .gitignore verbatim.
private/

# Press / social pack — generated by `make press-pack` from
# private/launch_pack/*.md. Lives in the local Google Drive working
# directory only; NEVER committed to the public repo (it's launch-prep
# material, not part of the report).
press-pack/

# Deeper private outreach / article workbook generated from
# private/dissemination/*. Lives locally only and is never committed or
# exported to the public evidence repo.
dissemination-pack/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only orchestration files seeded from general-repo for offline
# convenience. The canonical instances live at
# `general-repo/{methodology,scripts,agent_briefs,templates,Makefile,...}`
# and are the ones the publication pipeline actually uses (the build /
# verify gates are run from general-repo with `PUB=<this-repo>`). The
# seeded copies in this tree are reference-only and must not enter the
# publication's git history, matching the gas-tax v3.2.5 published-tree
# shape. See `methodology/public_private_boundary_protocol.md` for the
# canonical list of public-disallowed paths.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
POLICY_DOCS.md
Makefile
agent_briefs/
methodology/
policy_docs/
scripts/
templates/
.github/
research/

# Seeded reference docs in docs/ — copied from general-repo/docs/ at seed
# time for local convenience but not part of the publication's content.
# The publication's docs/ is populated at publish time by
# scripts/publish_pages.py (rendered HTML + Pages assets), which is what
# gas-tax's docs/ tracked tree looks like.
docs/agent_deployment.md
docs/brand_guide.md
docs/chart-spec.md
docs/cli_agent_calls.md
docs/content_exemplars.md
docs/currency_and_units.md
docs/design_system.md
docs/github_repo_pattern.md
docs/github_repo_presentation_contract.md
docs/methodology.md
docs/operator_runbook.md
docs/verification-standards.md
docs/workflow.md

# Seeded chart scaffolding — _template.py and values.py are seeder
# convenience copies. The publication-specific chart scripts that
# will land later use the format charts/NN_<descriptor>.py (mirrors
# gas-tax). charts/style.py is the framework stylesheet and IS tracked.
charts/_template.py
charts/values.py

# Seeded private review templates in final/ — these are filled in at
# release time and their content stays private (each file says so on
# line 1). The seeded skeletons are not part of the publication's
# git history.
final/human_signoff.md
final/public_boundary_review.md

# Stage A/B/C/D/E review outputs — private working artefacts per
# methodology/public_private_boundary_protocol.md. The disallowed-
# public list includes final/review_*.md, final/reviews/,
# final/synthesis.md, final/p0_p1_carryover.md.
final/review_*.md
final/reviews/
final/synthesis.md
final/p0_p1_carryover.md
